      "assistant_text": "The [[write-journal]] page describes the **Guarded Write Journal**, which is a mechanism that journals file state before making changes. Here\u0027s what it covers:\n\n**Purpose**: Before the guarded tool executor overwrites any file, it records that file\u0027s prior state \u2014 either its previous content (if it existed) or a note that it didn\u0027t exist \u2014 into an in-memory write journal.\n\n**Rollback functionality**: If the agent run fails for any reason (turn cap exceeded, unrecoverable error, or all writes denied), the journal can roll every recorded write back in reverse order by:\n- Restoring previous content for files that existed before\n- Deleting files that were newly created\n\n**Transaction semantics**: This provides all-or-nothing semantics for writes without needing a database transaction \u2014 the journal itself acts as the transaction log, kept in process memory for the duration of one run.\n\nThe page also notes that the Query agent never actually uses the journal\u0027s rollback capability since it has no write tool at all, though the journal type exists in the shared agent runtime library.",
      "input_tokens": 2595,
      "output_tokens": 235
    }
